@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using SpaceSails.Core
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE SCUTTLE EPITAPH, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION: not one character of the block below changed. Every page member
    the markup reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME — the fields keep their leading underscore, the
    methods keep their signature as a delegate — so the block could be lifted out and dropped back in without
    a rewrite, and the test suite's fifty-eight source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as they read
    it when it lived in the page.

    The `@if (_scuttleEpitaph is { } epitaph)` that used to open this block stays in Map.razor. That is
    deliberate and not laziness: it keeps the page's own paint order legible in one place, and it keeps this
    component UNRENDERED while the card is closed, so nothing about what the game costs per frame moved.

    IHandleEvent is copied from the page (Map.Sim.cs) because it is load-bearing: Blazor re-renders the whole
    component after every event by default, and the page turns that off — the HUD's refresh is owned by
    OnTick's 200 ms throttle. A child that did not repeat the override would put an automatic render back on
    every click inside this card.

    ScuttleEpitaphCard.razor.css carries no rules. It exists to give this component Map.razor.css's OWN css
    scope (pinned in SpaceSails.Client.csproj), so every `.scuttle-epitaph-text`/`.scuttle-art` rule the page
    already had goes on matching these elements. #251 item 3 is where the rules themselves move.
*@
@* ── THE PAGE'S OWN NOTE ON THIS SURFACE, moved here with it (#251 item 1) and not touched by a
   word: it is the paragraph that stood above this block in Map.razor. It sits ABOVE the fence, not
   inside it, so that a source guard slicing the block by text goes on reading markup and not prose.
   ── *@
    @* #488 · WHAT YOU HEARD ON THE WAY OUT. Owner: "some kind of pop-up with gen AI about hearing clawing
       of horrible sounds when we went :-D … a confirmation that we did something that made a difference."
       CONFIRMATION WITHOUT REVELATION — the instrument never once said what was in there, and neither does
       this. You know there was something. You know it is not out here any more. That is all you get. *@

@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="view-object-backdrop" @onclick="() => Dismiss(CloseScuttleEpitaph)">
            <OverlayShell class="vent-board scuttle-epitaph" StopClicks="true"
                          Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare" Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.Close"
                          DismissClass="view-object-close" DismissFace="@(_scuttleHeardIt ? "Sit with that" : "Log it")"
                          OnClose="() => Dismiss(CloseScuttleEpitaph)">
                <div class="view-object-title">☢ SHE IS GONE</div>
                <img class="scuttle-art" src="art/scuttle-she-goes.jpg" alt=""
                     onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
                <div class="scuttle-epitaph-text @(_scuttleHeardIt ? "heard" : "")">@epitaph</div>
            </OverlayShell>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@

@code {
    /// <summary>The sentence the ship's end wrote, bound out of the page's `_scuttleEpitaph`.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string epitaph { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>Was anything still alive aboard when she went. Names the page's own field.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool _scuttleHeardIt { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The page's `Dismiss(Action)` — the one way out every card in this game uses.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Func<Action, Task> Dismiss { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The page's `CloseScuttleEpitaph()`, handed on as the action `Dismiss` runs.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action CloseScuttleEpitaph { get; set; } = default!;

    // The page's own event dispatch, repeated: no automatic re-render per event. See the header.
    Task IHandleEvent.HandleEventAsync(EventCallbackWorkItem callback, object? arg) => callback.InvokeAsync(arg);
}
